<article class="env-lemma" id="01P8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01P8">Lemma <span data-tag="01P8">28.19.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $f \in \Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$. Assume $X$ is quasi-compact and quasi-separated and assume that $X_ f$ is affine. Then the canonical morphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  j : X \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X))  \]
</div>
  <p> from Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01I1" data-tag="01I1">26.6.4</a> induces an isomorphism of $X_ f = j^{-1}(D(f))$ onto the standard affine open $D(f) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X))$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is clear as $j$ induces an isomorphism of rings $\Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)_ f \to \mathcal{O}_ X(X_ f)$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/01P7" data-tag="01P7">28.18.1</a> above. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>